{"overview":{"Symbol":"EIKN","Name":"Eikon Therapeutics, Inc.","Description":"Eikon Therapeutics, Inc., operates as a clinical biopharmaceutical company in the United States. It develops medicines to address serious unmet medical needs. Its products include EIK1001, a systemically administered TLR 7/8 dual-agonist designed to activate innate and adaptive immune anti-tumor responses; EIK1003 and EIK1004, which are selective PARP1 inhibitors in ovarian, breast, prostate, and pancreatic cancers and, specifically with the brain-penetrant; EIK1004 to address brain metastases and primary brain malignancies; EIK1005, a potent WRN helicase inhibitor and anti-tumor agent for MSI-high tumors; and EIK1006, a clinical candidate and next-generation androgen receptor antagonist with activity against multiple clinically emergent variants of androgen receptor. The company was incorporated in 2019 and is based in Millbrae, California.","CIK":"","Exchange":"NasdaqGS","Currency":"USD","Country":"United States","Sector":"Healthcare","Industry":"Biotechnology","Address":"230 Harriet Tubman Way, Millbrae, CA, 94030, United States","FiscalYearEnd":"","LatestQuarter":"","MarketCapitalization":"453140320","EBITDA":"-310081984","PERatio":"","PEGRatio":"","BookValue":"10.172","DividendPerShare":"","DividendYield":"","EPS":"-6.32","RevenuePerShareTTM":"","ProfitMargin":"0","OperatingMarginTTM":"0","ReturnOnAssetsTTM":"","ReturnOnEquityTTM":"","RevenueTTM":"","GrossProfitTTM":"","DilutedEPSTTM":"-6.32","QuarterlyEarningsGrowthYOY":"","QuarterlyRevenueGrowthYOY":"","AnalystTargetPrice":"24.8","TrailingPE":"","ForwardPE":"-1.3532128","PriceToSalesRatioTTM":"","PriceToBookRatio":"0.822847","EVToRevenue":"","EVToEBITDA":"-0.63","Beta":"","52WeekHigh":"17.4","52WeekLow":"7.9","50DayMovingAverage":"10.2556","200DayMovingAverage":"11.61069","SharesOutstanding":"54138628","DividendDate":"","ExDividendDate":"","DebtToEquity":"46.276"},"daily":{"Meta Data":{"1. Information":"Daily Time Series (Yahoo Fina